2\\sqrt{(3-6)\\times (1-3)} & = \\\\ 2\\sqrt{(-3)\\times (-2)} & = \\\\ 2\\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we approximate the value of the radical using a calculator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & ≈‭‭‭2.449\\,490\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places.\n\nFinally, we approximate the value of the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{6} & ≈ \\\\ 2(2.449\\,490) & ≈ \\\\ 4.898\\,98 & ≈ \\\\ 4.899\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482513 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078452 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "985d535d-1f51-578d-bb43-a7940cb01fa6" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Radical Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a791971-c0af-5b44-9234-69c51ab2a6c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481883} {:answer/id #uuid "6ede240d-6358-55b6-9cf4-b903ea2291a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482031} {:answer/id #uuid "a805033e-a7ac-519f-b33f-976141e7d52a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}-9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482172} {:answer/id #uuid "ba1ccd6c-cca7-5e3e-8208-780deb7db979" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}-1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482218} {:answer/id #uuid "e090c643-e386-5c56-8d35-64ec35e4b767" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a791971-c0af-5b44-9234-69c51ab2a6c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481883} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0387295-9fb7-5920-87f6-eab66a076f57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482471}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1c3c665d-7d8f-59dd-ac27-822edd107571" :question/math-academy-id "q-69301" :question/problem "$\\sqrt{5}÷(1-{3}^{2})=$" :question/worked-solution "To simplify the given expression, we use PEMDAS. In terms of the order of operations: \n\n- expressions underneath radicals are treated the same as parentheses\n\n- radicals themselves are treated as exponents\n\nTherefore, following the order of operations, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5}÷(1-{3}^{2}) & = \\\\ \\sqrt{5}÷(1-9) & = \\\\ \\sqrt{5}÷(-8) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{(-8)} & = \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482581 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078450 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "10c998ff-ed64-586c-898d-92b25f48125f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Expressions Containing Radicals and One or Two Additional Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79c01a83-b5d6-5769-bd3e-9071be86c070" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482056} {:answer/id #uuid "98a03a70-0f68-53dd-8f66-007f630f4929" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482134} {:answer/id #uuid "b3221abf-3137-573d-a169-ef9108202aa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482195} {:answer/id #uuid "c216d6d4-e126-5ff3-8529-49885caaa9eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482237} {:answer/id #uuid "d06a0e38-f6cc-5b53-9560-3b91aa3818ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482272}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79c01a83-b5d6-5769-bd3e-9071be86c070" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482056} :answer-field/id #uuid "719b405c-02b7-5abd-9fbb-e9f0c434b9e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482436}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b558035c-db2a-5cb8-b598-445d3a220fdc" :question/math-academy-id "q-99397" :question/problem "$\\sqrt{4÷({3}^{2}-5)}=$" :question/worked-solution "To simplify the given expression, we use PEMDAS. In terms of the order of operations: \n\n- expressions underneath radicals are treated the same as parentheses\n\n- radicals themselves are treated as exponents\n\nTherefore, following the order of operations, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{4÷({3}^{2}-5)} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{4÷(9-5)} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{4÷4} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{1} & = \\\\ 1 & \\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
